{title: 009 - Let All the World in Every Corner Sing}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #009 • LUCKINGTON • 11.4.7.6.6.6.11.4}
{lyricist: George Herbert}
{composer: Basil Harwood}
{key: Db}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 9}
{meta: tune LUCKINGTON}
{meta: meter 11.4.7.6.6.6.11.4}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Db]Let all [Ab/C]the [Bbm]world [Db/F]in [Gb]every [Ab7]corner [Ab/C]sing,
[Db]My God [Ebm]and King!
[Ab]The [Db/F]heavens [Ebm]are [Ab]not [Ab7]too [Db]high,
[Gb]His [Ebm]praise [Ab]may [Ab7]thither [Ab/C]fly,
[Db]The earth [Ebm]is not [Ab]too low,
[Db]His praises [Ab]there [Db]may [Bbm]grow.
[Db/F]Let all the [Gb]world [Ebm]in [Ab]every [Db/F]corner [Ab]sing,
[Db]My God and King!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Db]Let all [Ab/C]the [Bbm]world [Db/F]in [Gb]every [Ab7]corner [Ab/C]sing
[Db]My God [Ebm]and King!
[Ab]The [Db/F]church [Gb]with [Ab]psalms [Ab7]must [Db]shout
[Gb]No [Ebm]door [Ab]can [Ab7]keep [Db]them [Ab/C]out;
[Db]But, above [Ebm]all, [Ab]the heart
[Db]Must bear [Ebm]the [Ab]longest [Bbm]part
[Db/F]Let all the [Gb]world [Ebm]in [Ab]every [Db/F]corner [Ab]sing
[Db]My God and King!
{end_of_verse}
